{"lines":[{"c":1,"y":0.038159038090920583,"w":0.08250458399454752,"x":0.82102069498143559,"h":0.01694457627531154,"t":"Reading"},{"h":0.019021226758154763,"y":0.087209302599367322,"c":1,"t":"at all'. Professor of Psychology Timothy Bates, who has been trying to replicate Dweck's work,","w":0.81747573852539068,"x":0.067961159763512927},{"c":1,"t":"is finding that the results are repeatedly null. He notes that: 'People with a growth mindset don't","w":0.81941747029622392,"h":0.018895348284474811,"y":0.10610465143689773,"x":0.067961167666492961},{"x":0.067914571686498462,"c":1,"w":0.81368835449218735,"h":0.021426265633366248,"y":0.12259694832057777,"t":"cope any better with failure ... Kids with the growth mindset aren't getting better grades, either"},{"h":0.018895348284474811,"y":0.14098837218043703,"t":"before or after our intervention study.'","w":0.33009707132975258,"c":1,"x":0.067961176140948876},{"w":0.80582524617513029,"y":0.18161993766509354,"c":1,"x":0.056310677787659622,"h":0.016199376947040434,"t":"• Much of this criticism is not lost on Dweck, and she deserves great credit for responding to it"},{"c":1,"y":0.20058139544354181,"w":0.78834950764973954,"t":"and adapting her work accordingly. In fact, she argues that her work has been misunderstood","x":0.067961168410843598,"h":0.015988371899566256},{"t":"and misapplied in a range of ways. She has also expressed concerns that her theories are being","y":0.21498669546568538,"x":0.067914280139970723,"h":0.021951539939809139,"w":0.80399861653645843,"c":1},{"y":0.23691860453811708,"w":0.77475728352864581,"h":0.01744186068621012,"c":1,"x":0.067961163954374043,"t":"misappropriated in schools by being conflated with the self-esteem movementiẠFor me the"},{"t":"growth mindset is a tool for learning and improvement. It's not just a vehicle for making children","h":0.019050205979391777,"c":1,"x":0.067961173512907272,"w":0.82912618001302074,"y":0.25420560746153753},{"h":0.019855169492347224,"c":1,"t":"feel good.'","x":0.067370433089848469,"y":0.27238621087192916,"w":0.096438344319661473},{"c":1,"h":0.017584945702478483,"x":0.067961171857193303,"y":0.31090342649872826,"t":"But there is another factor at work here. The failure to translate the growth mindset into the","w":0.77669901529947916},{"y":0.32835939079489052,"t":"classroom might reflect a misunderstanding of the nature of teaching and learning itself.","h":0.020735938526759701,"c":1,"x":0.067904679772434987,"w":0.75155064900716151},{"w":0.79999999999999993,"c":1,"x":0.067961164951456307,"y":0.34883720918965166,"h":0.01751793121623102,"t":"Growth mindset supporters David Yeager and Gregory Walton claim that interventions should"},{"w":0.75533981323242194,"c":1,"y":0.36627906963707457,"h":0.017521553396064649,"t":"be delivered in a subtle way to maximise their effectiveness. They say that if adolescents","x":0.067961161170638135},{"y":0.38504672871815271,"x":0.067961155286629091,"t":"perceive a teacher's intervention as conveying that they are in need of help, this could undo its","c":1,"w":0.80388351440429706,"h":0.019023038442261164},{"w":0.14833794911702475,"c":1,"t":"intended effects.","y":0.40392272427857479,"h":0.017974361526631899,"x":0.065673224595448124},{"w":0.81941747029622392,"x":0.067961167672289088,"t":"A lot of what drives students is their innate beliefs and how they perceive themselves. There is a","c":1,"h":0.017557777571158173,"y":0.44174454811848296},{"t":"strong correlation between self-perception and achievement, but there is evidence to suggest that","h":0.017450011185025094,"c":1,"y":0.46074766334089645,"w":0.82524271647135417,"x":0.06796116592865227},{"y":0.47965116267781904,"t":"the actual effect of achievement on self-perception is stronger than the other way round. To stand","c":1,"x":0.067961173853050907,"w":0.82718444824218762,"h":0.017545098753361632},{"w":0.80388351440429673,"y":0.49844236730885261,"x":0.067961155324335415,"h":0.017546004892509681,"t":"up in a classroom and successfully deliver a good speech is a genuine achievement, and that is","c":1},{"h":0.019022022972225772,"w":0.69524820963541678,"c":1,"y":0.51554980388690252,"t":"likely to be more powerfully motivating than vague notions of 'motivation' itself.","x":0.067897425538348891},{"t":"Recent evidence would suggest that growth mindset interventions are not the elixir of student","w":0.79611648559570314,"h":0.01756049420603345,"y":0.55377906965468149,"c":1,"x":0.067961174577832059},{"x":0.066019423543952016,"w":0.80776697794596353,"h":0.017530609439837974,"c":1,"t":"learning that its proponents claim it to be. The growth mindset appears to be a viable construct","y":0.57258566973794123},{"h":0.021828988333728816,"y":0.58999009659355639,"c":1,"x":0.065983488160454531,"w":0.80396993001302086,"t":"in the lab, which, when administered in the classroom via targeted interventions, doesn't seem"},{"t":"to work. It is hard to dispute that having faith in the capacity to change is a good attribute for","w":0.79417475382486991,"h":0.017468122678382381,"x":0.066019424471060031,"c":1,"y":0.60901162817259613},{"t":"students. Paradoxically, however, that aspiration is not well served by direct interventions that","w":0.80194173177083339,"h":0.020379627976462089,"x":0.067961172853191365,"y":0.62790697621519009,"c":1},{"w":0.12083754221598307,"t":"try to instil it.","y":0.64591548006848043,"x":0.065798856154803839,"h":0.017910130818684866,"c":1},{"t":"Motivational posters and talks are often a waste of time, and might well give students a deluded","w":0.81359222412109389,"h":0.017587662337353649,"x":0.069902916968579323,"y":0.68459302314317572,"c":1},{"t":"notion of what success actually means. Teaching concrete skills such as how to write an effective","x":0.067961173840312195,"h":0.016199376947040434,"y":0.70342679156546062,"w":0.82718444824218751,"c":1},{"h":0.017499819128684146,"c":1,"x":0.06601941291412175,"w":0.78640777587890631,"t":"introduction to an essay then praising students' effort in getting there is probably a far better","y":0.72087227400187659},{"y":0.7383177568007907,"x":0.067961188517947829,"t":"way of improving confidence than telling them how unique they are, or indeed how capable they","w":0.8233009338378906,"h":0.019003115264797477,"c":1},{"x":0.067961156984998092,"h":0.017595812836168734,"w":0.79805826822916659,"c":1,"t":"are of changing their own brains. Perhaps growth mindset works best as a philosophy and not","y":0.75856697796805217},{"c":1,"x":0.067751787571997499,"t":"an intervention.","y":0.77636537067260203,"w":0.13836598714192705,"h":0.017350716754283568},{"t":"89","x":0.87572815632967849,"y":0.95494186058743424,"w":0.027184464136759456,"h":0.014534883112922281,"c":1}],"w":2400,"h":3209}